Z||000009||Leadfoot||06-29-2001||10:56 AM||||You are not going to see that kind of weight reduction.  The steel cradles don't even weight 100 lbs with the control arms attached.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lou_dias:<BR>[B]recreate our cradles in aluminum and drop 100 or 200 lbs off the rear end? [B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||lou_dias||06-29-2001||01:17 PM||||Really...damn.  All that weight and torque it has to support and it only weight 100lbs...?<P>Anybody with a loose cradle out there than can verify this?<P>So going alumninum on the cradle could save 46lbs and on the block another 47lbs.  How about an aluminum crossmember for the 84-87 front suspension?<P>Weight reduction has so many beneifts.||||reg||1
